Cyber Security Task 1 – Basic Network Scanning with Nmap

1. Introduction

This project was completed as part of the Oasis Infobyte Cyber Security Internship. The purpose of this task was to understand how network scanning can be performed using Nmap and how the results can be used to identify the network exposure of a system.

For this task, I used my Kali Linux virtual machine as the testing environment and performed the scans on my own system.

2. Objective

The main objectives of this task were:

* To verify the installation of Nmap.
* To perform a basic network scan.
* To identify available services and their versions.
* To perform operating system detection.
* To identify open, closed, and filtered ports.
* To understand the security meaning of the scan results.
* To document the findings in a clear and structured way.

