12. Ethical Considerations

Nmap can provide detailed information about systems and networks, so it should only be used on systems that the tester owns or has explicit permission to assess.

For this task, I used my own Kali Linux environment and performed the scans in a controlled environment.

I did not scan external websites, public servers, university networks, or other systems without authorization.

13. Conclusion

This task gave me practical experience with Nmap and basic network scanning. I performed a basic scan, service and version detection, OS detection, and an additional localhost scan.

The scans did not identify any open TCP ports on the tested targets. I also learned how Nmap reports ports as filtered or closed and how these results can be useful when reviewing the network exposure of a system.

Overall, the task helped me understand the basic process of network scanning and the importance of checking exposed services as part of a security assessment.
